>> A2: In a few paragraphs, describe your code for accessing the data >> stored
in the SPT about a given page.

Our implementation uses a hash table keyed by the virtual address
(page-aligned). When a page fault occurs, the handler calls find_spte. find_spte
creates a dummy entry and passes it to hash_find to return the corresponding
virtual address. 

Each struct supp_page_table_entry holds the necessary metadata to load a page.
If the entry exists, vm_page_fault_helper uses the stored type and file/swap
info to load the data. For VM_BIN/VM_FILE, it calls load_file to read from disk.
For VM_ANON it either fills a zero page or reads from the swap partition via
swap_in.

